[{"id":"fm-core2-2.70-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>A transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is represented by the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A=\\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;0\\\\0&amp;3\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>State the geometrical transformation that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> represents.</p></li><li><p>Find the eigenvalues of matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and their corresponding eigenvectors.</p></li><li><p>State any invariant lines of the transformation.</p></li><li><p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\det\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and give a geometrical interpretation of this value.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Stretch parallel to the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis scale factor 2 and stretch parallel to the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis scale factor 3</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;0\\\\0&amp;3\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}=\\lambda\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A-\\lambda\\mathbf I=\\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;0\\\\0&amp;3\\end{pmatrix}-\\lambda\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}2-\\lambda&amp;0\\\\0&amp;3-\\lambda\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\det(\\mathbf A-\\lambda\\mathbf I)=(2-\\lambda)(3-\\lambda)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2-\\lambda)(3-\\lambda)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\lambda=2\\text{ or }\\lambda=3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda_1=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A-3\\mathbf I=\\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;0\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;0\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}=0\\Rightarrow y=0\\text{ for any value of }x\\text{ so }\\mathbf v_1=\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda_2=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A-3\\mathbf I=\\begin{pmatrix}-1&amp;0\\\\0&amp;0\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}-1&amp;0\\\\0&amp;0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}=0\\Rightarrow -x=0\\text{ for any value of }y\\text{ so }\\mathbf v_2=\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\lambda_1=2,\\mathbf v_1=\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}\\text{ and }\\lambda_2=3,\\mathbf v_2=\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\det\\mathbf A=6\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so the area of the image has been enlargened by a factor of 6</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.70-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>A transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is represented by the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A=\\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;1\\\\1&amp;0\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>State the geometrical transformation that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> represents.</p></li><li><p>Find the eigenvalues of matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and their corresponding eigenvectors.</p></li><li><p>State any invariant lines of the transformation.</p></li><li><p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\det\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and give a geometrical interpretation of this value.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Reflection across the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;1\\\\1&amp;0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}=\\lambda\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A-\\lambda\\mathbf I=\\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;1\\\\1&amp;0\\end{pmatrix}-\\lambda\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}0-\\lambda&amp;1\\\\1&amp;0-\\lambda\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\det(\\mathbf A-\\lambda\\mathbf I)=(-\\lambda)(-\\lambda)-1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda^2-1=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\lambda=-1\\text{ or }\\lambda=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda_1=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A+\\mathbf I=\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;1\\\\1&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;1\\\\1&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}=0\\Rightarrow x=-y\\text{ so }\\mathbf v_1=\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\-1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda_2=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A-1\\mathbf I=\\begin{pmatrix}-1&amp;1\\\\1&amp;-1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}-1&amp;1\\\\1&amp;-1\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}=0\\Rightarrow -x+y=0\\text{ so }\\mathbf v_2=\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\lambda_1=-1,\\mathbf v_1=\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\-1\\end{pmatrix}\\text{ and }\\lambda_2=1,\\mathbf v_2=\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\det\\mathbf A=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so the area is preserved, but the orientation is reversed.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.70-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>A transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is represented by the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A=\\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;-1\\\\1&amp;0\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>State the geometrical transformation that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> represents.</p></li><li><p>Find the eigenvalues of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>By considering the eigenvalues and then geometrically, explain why there are not any invariant lines of the transformation.</p></li><li><p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\det\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and give a geometrical interpretation of this value.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Rotation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"90^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> anti-clockwise about the origin.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;-1\\\\1&amp;0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}=\\lambda\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A-\\lambda\\mathbf I=\\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;-1\\\\1&amp;0\\end{pmatrix}-\\lambda\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}0-\\lambda&amp;-1\\\\1&amp;0-\\lambda\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\det(\\mathbf A-\\lambda\\mathbf I)=(-\\lambda)(-\\lambda)+1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda^2+1=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\lambda=-i\\text{ or }\\lambda=i\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Since the eigenvalues are complex, there are no invariant lines.</p>","<p>Geometrically, since every line rotates, no real line maps onto itself.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\det\\mathbf A=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so the area and orientation is preserved.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.70-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>A transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is represented by the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A=\\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;0\\\\0&amp;-2\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the eigenvalues of matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and their corresponding eigenvectors.</p></li><li><p>State any invariant lines of the transformation.</p></li><li><p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\det\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and give a geometrical interpretation of this value.</p></li><li><p>Describe fully the transformation represented by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;0\\\\0&amp;-2\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}=\\lambda\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A-\\lambda\\mathbf I=\\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;0\\\\0&amp;-2\\end{pmatrix}-\\lambda\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}2-\\lambda&amp;0\\\\0&amp;-2-\\lambda\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\det(\\mathbf A-\\lambda\\mathbf I)=(2-\\lambda)(-2-\\lambda)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2-\\lambda)(-2-\\lambda)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\lambda=-2\\text{ or }\\lambda=2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda_1=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A+2\\mathbf I=\\begin{pmatrix}4&amp;0\\\\0&amp;0\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}4&amp;0\\\\0&amp;0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}=0\\Rightarrow 4x=0\\text{ so }\\mathbf v_1=\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda_2=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A-2\\mathbf I=\\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;0\\\\0&amp;-4\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;0\\\\0&amp;-4\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}=0\\Rightarrow -4y=0\\text{ so }\\mathbf v_2=\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\lambda_1=-2,\\mathbf v_1=\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}\\text{ and }\\lambda_2=2,\\mathbf v_2=\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\det\\mathbf A=-4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so the area is enlarged by factor of 4, and the orientation is reversed.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>The eigenvalues and eigenvectors tell us:</p>","<ul class=\"parts\"><li><p>A stretch of scale factor 2 in the direction <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>A stretch of scale factor 2 in the direction <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with a reflection in the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis</p></li></ul>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\" data-display=\"false\"></span> Enlargement of scale factor 2 and a reflection in the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.70-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>A transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is represented by the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A=\\frac15\\begin{pmatrix}13&amp;6\\\\6&amp;22\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the eigenvalues of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Determine the Cartesian equations of the two lines passing through the origin which are invariant under the transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Describe fully the transformation represented by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}\\frac{13}5&amp;\\frac65\\\\\\frac65&amp;\\frac{22}5\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}=\\lambda\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A-\\lambda\\mathbf I=\\begin{pmatrix}\\frac{13}5&amp;\\frac65\\\\\\frac65&amp;\\frac{22}5\\end{pmatrix}-\\lambda\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\frac{13}5-\\lambda&amp;\\frac65\\\\\\frac65&amp;\\frac{22}5-\\lambda\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\det(\\mathbf A-\\lambda\\mathbf I)=(\\frac{13}5-\\lambda)(\\frac{22}5-\\lambda)-\\frac{36}{25}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda^2-7\\lambda+10=(\\lambda-2)(\\lambda-5)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\lambda=2\\text{ or }\\lambda=5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda_1=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A-2\\mathbf I=\\begin{pmatrix}\\frac35&amp;\\frac65\\\\\\frac65&amp;\\frac{12}5\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}\\frac35&amp;\\frac65\\\\\\frac65&amp;\\frac{12}5\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}=0\\Rightarrow\\frac35x+\\frac65y=0\\text{ so }y=-\\frac12x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda_2=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A-5\\mathbf I=\\begin{pmatrix}-\\frac{12}5&amp;\\frac65\\\\\\frac65&amp;-\\frac35\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}-\\frac{12}5&amp;\\frac65\\\\\\frac65&amp;-\\frac35\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}=0\\Rightarrow-\\frac{12}5x+\\frac65y=0\\text{ so }y=2x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y=-\\frac12x\\text{ and }y=2x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>The eigenvalues and eigenvectors tell us:</p>","<ul class=\"parts\"><li><p>A stretch of scale factor 2 in the direction <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}2\\\\-1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>A stretch of scale factor 5 in the direction <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\2\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ul>","<p>They are perpendicular so there are no rotations or shears.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\" data-display=\"false\"></span> A stretch of scale factor 2 along <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-\\frac12x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and a stretch of scale factor 5 along <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.70-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>Under a linear transformation, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is mapped to the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(6,8)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><p>For the matrix representing <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Write down the eigenvector.</p></li><li><p>Write down the corresponding eigenvalue.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\begin{pmatrix}3\\\\4\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}6\\\\8\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}3\\\\4\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is an eigenvector.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.70-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>Under a linear transformation, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,-5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is mapped to the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-4,10)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><p>For the matrix representing <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Write down the eigenvector.</p></li><li><p>Write down the corresponding eigenvalue.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-2\\begin{pmatrix}2\\\\-5\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}-4\\\\10\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}2\\\\-5\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is an eigenvector.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.70-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>A transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is represented by the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A=\\begin{pmatrix}p&amp;q\\\\q&amp;p\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for non-zero constants <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\\neq q\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the eigenvalues and corresponding eigenvectors of matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> giving your answer in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Show that the invariant lines of the transformation are perpendicular.</p></li><li><p>Describe fully the transformation represented by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}p&amp;q\\\\q&amp;p\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}=\\lambda\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A-\\lambda\\mathbf I=\\begin{pmatrix}p&amp;q\\\\q&amp;p\\end{pmatrix}-\\lambda\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}p-\\lambda&amp;q\\\\q&amp;p-\\lambda\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\det(\\mathbf A-\\lambda\\mathbf I)=(p-\\lambda)(p-\\lambda)-q^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda^2-2\\lambda p+p^2-q^2=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(\\lambda-(p-q))(\\lambda-(p+q))=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\lambda=p-q\\text{ or }\\lambda=p+q\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda_1=p-q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A-(p-q)\\mathbf I=\\begin{pmatrix}q&amp;q\\\\q&amp;q\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}q&amp;q\\\\q&amp;q\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}=0\\Rightarrow qx+qy=0\\text{ so }\\mathbf v_1=\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\-1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda_2=p+q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A-(p+q)\\mathbf I=\\begin{pmatrix}-q&amp;q\\\\q&amp;-q\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}-q&amp;q\\\\q&amp;-q\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}=0\\Rightarrow -qx+qy=0\\text{ so }\\mathbf v_2=\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\lambda_1=p-q,\\mathbf v_1=\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\-1\\end{pmatrix}\\text{ and }\\lambda_2=p+q,\\mathbf v_2=\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Invariant lines are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Consider gradients: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-1\\times1=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so the invariant lines are perpendicular.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>The eigenvalues and eigenvectors tell us:</p>","<ul class=\"parts\"><li><p>A stretch of scale factor <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p-q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the direction <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\-1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>A stretch of scale factor <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p+q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the direction <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ul>","<p>They are perpendicular so there are no rotations or shears.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\" data-display=\"false\"></span> A stretch of scale factor <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p-q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> along <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and a stretch of scale factor <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p+q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> along <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.70-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>A transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is represented by the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A=\\begin{pmatrix}3&amp;1\\\\1&amp;3\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the eigenvalues of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Determine the Cartesian equations of the two lines passing through the origin which are invariant under the transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Describe fully the transformation represented by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}3&amp;1\\\\1&amp;3\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}=\\lambda\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A-\\lambda\\mathbf I=\\begin{pmatrix}3&amp;1\\\\1&amp;3\\end{pmatrix}-\\lambda\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}3-\\lambda&amp;1\\\\1&amp;3-\\lambda\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\det(\\mathbf A-\\lambda\\mathbf I)=(3-\\lambda)(3-\\lambda)-1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda^2-6\\lambda+8=(\\lambda-4)(\\lambda-2)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\lambda=2\\text{ or }\\lambda=4\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda_1=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A-2\\mathbf I=\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;1\\\\1&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;1\\\\1&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}=0\\Rightarrow x+y=0\\text{ so }y=-x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda_2=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A-4\\mathbf I=\\begin{pmatrix}-1&amp;1\\\\1&amp;-1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}-1&amp;1\\\\1&amp;-1\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}=0\\Rightarrow-x+y=0\\text{ so }y=x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y=-x\\text{ and }y=x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has eigenvalues 4 and 16</p>","<ul class=\"parts\"><li><p>A stretch of scale factor 4 in the direction <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\-1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>A stretch of scale factor 16 in the direction <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ul>","<p>They are perpendicular so there are no rotations or shears.</p>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> stretches along the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> by scale factor 4 and along the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> by scale factor 16</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.70-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>A transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is represented by the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A=\\begin{pmatrix}-10&amp;8\\\\-16&amp;14\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><p>Describe fully the transformation represented by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}-10&amp;8\\\\-16&amp;14\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}=\\lambda\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A-\\lambda\\mathbf I=\\begin{pmatrix}-10&amp;8\\\\-16&amp;14\\end{pmatrix}-\\lambda\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}-10-\\lambda&amp;8\\\\-16&amp;14-\\lambda\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\det(\\mathbf A-\\lambda\\mathbf I)=(-10-\\lambda)(14-\\lambda)+128\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda^2-4\\lambda-12=(\\lambda+2)(\\lambda-6)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\lambda=-2\\text{ or }\\lambda=6\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda_1=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A+2\\mathbf I=\\begin{pmatrix}-8&amp;8\\\\-16&amp;16\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}-8&amp;8\\\\-16&amp;16\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}=0\\Rightarrow-8x+8y=0\\text{ so }x=y\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda_2=6\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A-6\\mathbf I=\\begin{pmatrix}-16&amp;8\\\\-16&amp;8\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}-16&amp;8\\\\-16&amp;8\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}=0\\Rightarrow-16x+8y=0\\text{ so }y=2x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y=x\\text{ and }y=2x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has eigenvalues <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-2)^3=-8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6^3=216\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<ul class=\"parts\"><li><p>A stretch of scale factor <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the direction <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>A stretch of scale factor 216 in the direction <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\2\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ul>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> stretches along the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> by scale factor 8, with a change in orientation, and along the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> by scale factor 216 with orientation preserved.</p>"]}]